% in reverse-chronological order and that order is preserved on the site — the
% generator emits a `weight` from each entry's position in this file.
%
% Conventions:
%   featured = {true}   promotes an entry to the "Selected publications" block
%                       on the homepage. Seven are currently flagged — the set
%                       that the university bio page listed as selected.
%   and others          marks a truncated author list. It renders as an
%                       ellipsis in the right position and is kept out of the
%                       JSON-LD author array. The source list was itself
%                       truncated for many multi-author papers, so these are
%                       not complete author lists.
%   url = {...}         used only where the source gave no DOI. DOIs were never
%                       constructed by guessing from a publisher URL.
%   abstract = {...}    optional; a real "## Abstract" section in the body.
%                       VERBATIM only, never retyped: fill it with
%                       scripts/fetch_abstract.py (copies from Crossref where
%                       reuse is permitted) or paste the publisher's text;
%                       check with `scripts/fetch_abstract.py --check KEY`.
%   abstract_kind = {opening}  the entry has no published abstract (letter,
%                       comment, review); `abstract` then holds the verbatim
%                       first paragraph, headed "Opening paragraph".
%   license = {...}     licence of the published version: "CC BY 4.0" etc. or
%                       "publisher (subscription)"; from Crossref via
%                       `scripts/fetch_abstract.py --licenses`. Decides what may
%                       be shown in full (see .claude/HANDOFF.md).
%   (Verification status, sources and legal basis of abstracts and notes are
%    tracked outside this file, in .claude/maintenance/publications.json —
%    see scripts/check_site.py.)
%   significance = {...} a short, AI-generated "why it matters" note (never
%                       sourced from an API) rendered under the abstract.
%                       Present for all entries.
